# How to cite Askurious. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository".
# RWTH Aachen University holds the rights in the code (§ 69b UrhG) and licenses it under EUPL-1.2 (LICENSE, NOTICE).
# The version is the release tag (docs/releases.md); this file names no version, so it stays right between releases.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Askurious in your research, please cite it as below and name the release you used
  (for example 2026.10.0). RWTH Aachen University holds the rights in the software.
type: software
title: Askurious
abstract: >-
  Askurious is a web platform for planning, building, fielding and analysing surveys, live polls, interview guides
  and diary studies in research and teaching.
authors:
